{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph that generic code can fill: the undirected counterpart of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"MutableDirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", with the members a reader needs to build a graph by key."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"text":"> : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertices","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8VerticesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertices-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each vertex has a key: its index in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Vertices.Index == Int"},{"text":"). On the dense","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"representations (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedAdjacencyList"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pseudograph"},{"text":") the key is the vertex’s slot.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Every conformer satisfies these laws:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_key(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"vertices.firstIndex(of: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"_vertex(atKey:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is its inverse."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_insertVertex(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" appends a vertex, which must not already be one, and returns its key,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices.endIndex"},{"type":"text","text":" before the call. Keys of other vertices do not change."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"_insertEdge(fromKey: u, toKey: v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" inserts the edge, stored as "},{"code":"UndirectedEdge(u, v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that orientation, and returns its position. On a simple graph ("},{"code":"UndirectedAdjacencyList","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an edge already present, in either orientation, is not inserted again, and its position is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned. Inserting an edge changes no key."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"remove(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" removes "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and every edge at it, returning the removed instance. "},{"code":"remove(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"